{title: As I Rise To Walk With Him}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 103}

Verse 1
[D]Except [D]a [F#m]seed be [G]returned to the earth,
[Gm]There to [D]die to itself,
[Bm]And [Bm7]yet to [Em]find its rebirth,
[A]So [A7]I [D]now testify
[F#m]I am [G]born from [Gm7]above,
Trusting [D]in the [A7]Savior's love!

Chorus
[Bm7]As [B]I die [A](as I die) to [C#m]my sin [D](to my sin)
I [B]am raised [E]unto life [A]everlasting with Him.
Praise the Lord [Bm7]for His [F#]love
[F#m]Shining [G]down from above
[Gm7]As I [D]rise to [A]walk with Him.

Verse 2
[D]No [D]more a slave [F#m]to [F#]the sin [G]that I knew,
[Gm7]For [D]the Lord's cleansing [Bm7]power
Now has [E]made [Bm]all things [A]new.
Washed [D]away is the old
[F#]By the [G]blood of the Lamb;
[Gm]By His grace [D]alone [A]I stand!
[G](Repeat Chorus)
As [G]I die [A7](as I die) to my [D]sin (to my sin)
[D]I [G]am raised [E]unto life everlasting [A]with Him.
Praise the Lord [D]for His [F#]love
[F#m]Shining [G]down from above
[G7]As I [D]rise to [A]walk with [D]Him.
[D](Banjo and fiddle solo)
[G](Repeat Chorus)
[D]As [A]I die (as I die) to my sin (to my sin)
I am raised unto life everlasting with Him.
Praise [D]the Lord for His [F#m]love
Shining [G]down from above
[Gm7]As I [D]rise to [A]walk with [D]Him.
